.TH MODBUS-FAKE-CLI 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
modbus-fake-cli \- console-style control session for the fake inverter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modbus-fake-cli
.RI [ options ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
An interactive console on the \fBmodbus-fake-inverter\fR JSON-lines
control server: on connect it probes the fake and greets you with the
profile, the uptime, the clock and the battery state; the prompt shows the
connected port (\fBfake-inverter:5502 >\fR). TAB completes commands,
settings and their values (the listings group the settings under the
registry's own groups \(em ungrouped rows render bare, no header \(em, with
[values] beside, descriptions aligned); \fB?\fR prints
the same in any position; \fBhelp <setting>\fR explains one; \fBshutdown\fR
asks \fBProceed with shutdown? [confirm]\fR first.
.PP
While idle the session sends wire pings every 55 s; when the connection
dies, the console retries (default 3 times, 10 s apart) and resumes on the
first success. The session is audited with the \fBCLI\fR prefix; the wire
commands are audited once, by the server.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-control\-port
control server target: unix socket path or TCP port on 127.0.0.1,
auto\-detected (default: /tmp/fake\-inverter\-5502.socket; env CTL when
unset) — same flag as the fake itself
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " N"
socket timeout in seconds (default 5.0)
.TP
.BI \-\-reconnect " N"
when the connection dies (an unanswered ping, a reset, a timeout), retry
this many times before giving up; 0 = off (default 3)
.TP
.BI \-\-reconnect\-wait " N"
seconds between the reconnect attempts (default 10.0)
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token
control auth token for TCP (env CONTROL_TOKEN); a file:<path> value
reads the first line of an owner\-only 0600 file
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-log
audit trail: a file path or \- for stdout; default: the XDG state home
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-max\-mb " N"
rotate the audit log at this size in MB, keeping 3 backups; 0 = off
(default 10.0)
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-files " N"
rotated audit backups to keep (default 3)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audit\-log
disable the audit trail (default: off)


.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLI_KEEPALIVE
idle ping interval, seconds (default \fB55\fR); \fB0\fR = off.
.TP
.B CTL ", " CONTROL_TOKEN
the default control target and TCP token.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
the session ended cleanly.
.TP
.B 1
connection or control error.
.TP
.B 2
command-line misuse.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-fake-inverter (1),
.BR modbus-fake-ctl (1)
